    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356-a2">

                <pb facs="0474" n="366" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg366"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2, in No. 141.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Durham to Mr. Lespinasse.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of a memorandum concerning the outrage perpetrated on Mr. Frederick Mevs, over
                    your signature, bearing even date, which you ask me to verify.</p>
                <p>I beg leave to remark that there seems to have escaped your attention my express
                    statement that my instructions do not permit me to make any written
                    communication to your Government at this stage.</p>
                <p>You will, I am sure, Mr. Minister, accept this violation of my instructions as a
                    demonstration of the high consideration with which I continue to be your humble
                    and obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John S. Durham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
